{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nThe issue and PR lists only refresh on `r` (the runs column and watch mode poll); with agents opening issues and PRs all day the lists go stale quickly. Polling `gh issue list` / `gh pr list` outright would spend GraphQL points, so the refresh should be driven by a **free** change check.\n\n## Spec\n\n1. **Change detection (0 points)** — every `github-poll-interval`, while the GitHub page is shown, run one conditional REST request: `gh api -H \"If-None-Match: <last ETag>\" repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues?state=all&sort=updated&direction=desc&per_page=1`. A `304 Not Modified` (measured: `gh api -i` returns it, exit 0) costs nothing and ends the tick. A `200` — the ETag or the top item's `updated_at` changed — triggers the existing `gh issue list` + `gh pr list` (+ stacks) refetch (~1 point in total). `/issues` covers issues and PRs alike.\n2. **Governed like every other poll** — follows the #168 refresh scale (idle ×6, under 20 % ×2, stopped under 5 % or with `github-auto-refresh \"off\"`) and the rate-limit backoff; no new config node.\n3. **Selection and state survive** — the lists keep the selected item by number (`set_items`), focus and search state stay; closed issues and merged PRs drop out.\n4. **Shown detail follows** — when the changed item is the one open in the detail pane, its detail (body, comments, checks) is refetched through the watch-mode path.\n5. **Status bar** — `lists 12s ago` (the Projects page's `board 12m ago` style) and a brief `↻ updated` when a refresh was triggered.\n6. **Fixtures / tests** — the conditional request joins `vig fixtures record`; unit tests cover ETag → 304 → 200 transitions; the fixture integration test checks that a 304 does not refetch.\n\n## Cost\n\n720 conditional requests per hour at the default 5 s — free while nothing changes; ~1 point per detected change. Note: project field edits (Status moves, dates) do not bump an issue's `updated_at`, so this check does not cover the Projects board — see the companion issue.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-09T07:13:34Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":177,"state":"OPEN","title":"GitHub: auto-refresh the issue and PR lists on a free change check"}
